{
  "_readme": "HAND-KEPT. The illustrated sprites build.py merges into content/art/pixel/pixel-art-manifest.json (schema v2) beside the generated pixel placeholders. The PNGs are not built here: they are exported from the masters in content/art/source/<id>/ (enemies: content/art/source/enemies/<type>/<region variant>/) by Tooling/ArtLab/scripts/export_ingame.py. Per sprite: Name (unique in the manifest), File (relative to content/art/pixel/), Category, Label, ArtKey (the species' ArtKey in content/data/Creatures/beast-roster.json, or the enemy's in content/data/Encounters/enemy-library.json, names it), PivotX/PivotY (the feet, px from the frame's top-left, as export_ingame.py prints them) and WorldHeight: the in-game height from the feet to the top of the art, in world units (1 = one hex column step; the pixel placeholders stand about 0.75 tall). WorldHeight is the species-size knob: build.py derives PixelsPerUnit = (PivotY - the art's top row) / WorldHeight, so a new value needs only a rebuild. FrameWidth/FrameHeight are read from the PNG; Filter is linear and Premultiplied false (straight-alpha PNGs, premultiplied on load). Enemies (Category enemy) also name AccentFile: the element-accent overlay export_ingame.py --accent-mask wrote beside the sprite (same frame); build.py lists it as its own sprite <Name>_accent and gives the base Accent (that name), AccentElement (the element the art is drawn in: Verdant Hollow art is Nature) and AccentNative (the accent's own colour, #rrggbb, as export_ingame.py printed it; the split is baked against it, so change it only with a re-export). The viewer draws the base, then the overlay multiplied by the unit's element colour: AccentNative for AccentElement (or no element), else the palette colour ElementAccents names for that element. An enemy's WorldHeight follows the lineup rule (docs/design/presentation-and-vfx.md, Enemy sizes): 0.95 of its footprint's width wide (one hex; the Champion's triangle 1.75, the Giant's Hex7 flower 2.5; the swarm units 0.55 of a hex), capped at 1.7 tall for a one-hex unit. Painted (the art slots of docs/art/hollow-art-slots.md that are not characters standing on a tile: battle backdrops, painted VFX frames, the skill-icon frame and rarity rings, painted skill icons): Name, File, Category, Label, optional ArtKey, WorldWidth (the world units the frame spans across: PixelsPerUnit = FrameWidth / WorldWidth, so a repaint at another resolution draws the same size), optional PivotU/PivotV (the pivot as fractions of the frame, default its centre) and Premultiplied (default false); one frame, Filter linear. Until the art lane paints a slot its file is a placeholder from Tooling/PixelArt/painted_placeholders.py.",
